{{also|Westen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|wēsten||a desert, waste}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*wōstinjō||a waste, wilderness}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*wāsto-||empty, wasted}}. Cognate with {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|woastyn||desert|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|frs|-}} {{term|wustenej||desert|lang=frs}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|woestijn||desert|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|gâtine||wasteland, moor|lang=fr}} (, from {{etyl|gem|-}}), {{etyl|gmh|-}} {{term|wuostinne||desert, wilderness|lang=gmh}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Wüste||desert|lang=de}}). More at {{l|en|westy}}, {{l|en|waste}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[waste]], [[wasteland]]; [[desert]].

